This project also adapts portions of pi-openai-server-compaction:
https://github.com/algal/pi-openai-server-compaction
Copyright (c) 2026 Alexis Gallagher, licensed under the MIT License.
Taken from PR #7 head 9ea79cb89fecca4c7ab09739530ee78a654cd32f (refs/pull/7/head),
read at that commit -- not from a published tarball.

The pending-warning stash in src/pending-warning.ts, and the reason it exists -- that a
before-compaction ui.notify is destroyed by the post-compaction chat rebuild, so an
operator-visible warning has to be re-emitted afterwards as a ui.setWidget widget -- are
adapted from that project's src/state.ts and src/index.ts. The finding was re-verified
against this project's own pinned @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent 0.81.1 rather than
adopted on the upstream author's word.

The per-target retry layer in src/retry.ts is also adapted from that project's
src/remote-compaction.ts at the same PR #7 head: the RemoteCompactionError shape (here
RouteAttemptError), the retryable/non-retryable classifier pair whose quota pattern vetoes
retry, retryAfterDelayMs's preference for retry-after-ms over retry-after with an HTTP-date
fallback, the 60-second ceiling past which a provider's requested delay is failed fast
rather than slept, and sleepForRemoteCompactionRetry's abort-inside-the-sleep with
removeEventListener cleanup and a synthesized AbortError. Nothing else from that project is
used here: its WebSocket transport, provider takeover, Codex identity headers and
remote-compaction protocol are all out of scope for a router.

